know many of you in the  room use as part of your data sets to  drive your business models to convince  investors to invest and even just to get  a better feel for the competitive  landscape out there but before we delve  into and identifying our Award winners  this year I'd like to try and give you a  little bit of insight with regard to the  very latest fiber-to-the-home council  panorama which is the very most up to  date and information I can see all the  phones  camera phones coming out straight away  and the session this afternoon and I  think it's session 8 if I remember  correctly will be going through all of  the detail of this you'll have plenty of  opportunity to grab some snap static but  I think some of the key things that are  worth noting at this point is as I  mentioned earlier during the opening  keynote we've now got 36.4% of european  homes that can avail of a full fiber  connection which is a fantastic  achievement and that's on the back of a  lot of momentum which is only continuing  to gain pace as we go forward and with  40 set 40% as subscriptions and across  those fibre footprints where they're  available again as I mentioned earlier  the consumer awareness is increasing out  there all the time which we think is  particularly important we've seen the UK  market enter into the permit panorama  with a level of force they're already up  to 1.3 percent of household  subscriptions today and those  subscriptions are up by 83 percent which  is a big achievement it's worth noting  that Spain Spain has surpassed Sweden so  Sweden for a long long time has held up  position up towards the very top of the  panorama Spain because of all the effort  they've been putting in over the last  couple of years have really massively  grown their market share with regard to  homes connected and subscribers on those  networks and Spain has done really well  now to display Sweden on that front so  no pressure no sweetener you just need  to re-engage and up the game 