tlemen I'm delighted to be  able to announce that the 2019 winner of  the individual fiber-to-the-home Council  award is Dana Toback the CEO of hyper  optic  now unfortunately Dana's not able to  join us today  I actually saw Dana at Mobile World  Congress there week and a half ago  thereabouts and I can oh I can only say  she was exhausted I think the level of  activity that's been going on within her  business I know they've been fundraising  etc has really taken its toll and Dana  is actually she's out of the office at  the moment due to illness and I think a  lot of that stems from the amount of  activity that she's had to deal with and  thankfully Pascal Costard their CTO has  joined us today and Pascal is going to  accept the award on behalf of Dana  please give a warm welcome to Pascal  Pascal  congratulations to Dana as well thank  you thank you very much our next award  is the operator award and this year's  winner of the operator award many of us  know this operator for their activities  and as an incumbent however despite  their incumbents paid the incumbent  parents massive activities in  fiber-to-the-home  this is not the reason that they were  selected as a challenger this operator  is proven that independent of their  parent they've been able to really shake  up the fiber market in which they  operate with an objective of reaching 16  million households by 2020 with its own  fiber to the home network and  incidentally this operator is one of the  most profitable of the subsidiaries  within its parent which says a lot about  the business model for fibre to the home  that they're building ash they are  positioning themselves for 5g also and  their fiber assets will have a huge role  to play as per as part of that so ladies  and gentlemen I'm delighted to announce  that the winner of the fiber at home  council operator award  is if I can get our clicker to click is  are in Spain please give a warm  congratulations to our in Spain curve a  pass a layer of orange group the deputy  CEO and chairman is going to join me on  stage and accept the award on behalf of  orange group congratulations well done  thank you very much fantastic thank you  well done again Cheers just to says that  as that's been expressed we are quite  proud to to win this award as a  challenger even if it's part of a bigger  group bazoo as a challenge with this  group to get the cap extra Spain as well  we'll be in tough France trying to  capture most of the capex forints group  we are we have been fighting year after  year to be able to build this  infrastructure but also to share it with  others as I try to explain so it's a mix  of our own infrastructure plus  cooperation plus wholesale and I see  it's a success we need to have for  building the infrastructure of tomorrow  in this continent thank you  so ladies and gentlemen this concludes  our individual and operator awards for  this year please do remember we also  have the inaugural charles cow award  tomorrow a 3 p.m. so please do try and  come along to see who's going to be the  first winner of that very very special  award we break now for lunch and  activities resume per the normal  schedule at 2:30 p.m. thank you very  much  you

